icipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, leadership, but unorganized, not good at criticism, not open to new ideas. Candidate B: conscientious, stress handling, but uncooperative. Candidate D not discussed.\n\nWe need to consider criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability. C strong on reliability, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation (positive atmosphere). Communication difficulty is a concern but maybe mitigable. A strong on anticipation, leadership, but unorganized and not open to criticism, which affect reliability and adaptability. B strong on stress resilience, but uncooperative. D unknown.\n\nThus C seems strongest overall. So we may shift to Candidate C. Provide argument referencing Agent 3's points and our own notes. Provide evidence: 100% reliable, correct decisions quickly, positive crew atmosphere, excellent attention. Concern: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Argue that these are less critical than A's unorganized and not open to criticism, and can be mitigated. So we vote for C.\n\nWe must produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: concise, argumentative, referencing discussion, stating recommendation for C, using explicit facts. Then METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
